dosbox-x Borland-Clipper-Microsoft
==================================


USEFUL LINKS
------------

* https://winworldpc.com/
* https://archive.org


INSTALLATION
------------

You can install dosbox-x by means of

    sudo apt install dosbox-x

Then unzip this zip file to your ~ directory


CONFIGURATION
-------------

To configure the dosbox-x, you can edit the file

    ./dosbox-x.conf

Note that the definitions of COM1..COM9 are for test purposes only (for the moment).

To use the definition of LPT1..LPT9 the program prt1403 must be installed. This program is open source and can be found at https://github.com/Pynckels/prt1403

STARTUP
-------

To start this retro programming dosbox: execute (run) the file

    ./dosbox-x.sh

This can be done from the command line interface (terminal) or from the file manager in the graphical user interface.


Installed products
------------------

* Borland Turbo Assembler  1.0  1988
* Borland Turbo Basic      1.1  1987
* Borland Turbo C          2.0  1988
* Borland Turbo Debugger   1.0  1988
* Borland Turbo Pascal     3.0  1986
* Borland Turbo Pascal     4.0  1987
* Borland Turbo Pascal     5.0  1988
* Borland Turbo Prolog     2.0  1988

* Computer Associates Clipper       5.2  1987
* Computer Associates Clipper Tools 3.0  19??

* Microsoft Assembler  6.11  1993
* Microsoft C          6.00  1990
* Microsoft Cobol      5.00  1993
* Microsoft Fortran    5.10  1991
* Microsoft Pascal     4.00  1988
* Microsoft QuickBasic 4.50  1988

* Volkswriter III  1.0  1985
* Wordperfect      5.1  1989


